{
  "about": "Layers.hitStack on both phones: the page's elements back to front, and what a fingertip touchRadius round at each probe lands on, top-most first. A hidden element is never listed; a group is one row, \"group:<id>\", listed where its top-most touched member is, with its shown members (a group left with one shown member is that member's row); a member of a cropped group is touched only where the crop shows it; anything thinner than twice the radius is touched as if grown to that about its centre, a turned one in its turned frame. Probes stay clear of edges, so the iPhone's 4-unit slack does not matter. A probe's own touchRadius overrides the top-level one. behind gives Alt+Tab's next row for a selection: the row under the one holding it, round to the top past the bottom, the top when none holds it, null when there is no other row.",
